-- REGRESSION PIN for RUN-XMOD-039 F1 (`core__foo`), and one half of the
-- "FEATURE LANDED + UNRELATED CODE STILL BEHAVES" pair this corpus was missing.
-- Promoted verbatim from the slice-breaker's `pD` probe.
--
-- 🚨 READ WHAT THIS ASSERTS BEFORE CHANGING IT. Nothing here exercises the
-- #1337 feature at all: there is NO `export import` anywhere, no re-export hop,
-- one dependency, one alias import. That is the entire point. AGENTS.md names
-- this the single most expensive defect shape in the tree -- "your feature works
-- perfectly and something unrelated breaks" -- and it is invisible to every
-- fixture that exercises the feature, because those all pass.
--
-- WHAT BROKE. The first version of the #1337 fix decided "is this dependency
-- scheme key already the symbol the reference will look up?" by asking whether
-- the key carried SOME loaded module's mangle prefix -- a pure STRING-SHAPE
-- question. It seeded that set with `"core"`, and `mangledName "core" "" ==
-- "core__"`, so this file's perfectly ordinary `core__foo` was misread as
-- already-mangled, left un-rebound, and rejected:
--   `main.mdk:6:7: Unbound variable: O.core__foo`, exit 1 on check AND run AND
--   build (plus a cascaded `Ambiguous instance for 'Display'`). No binary.
-- The base binary compiled this file and printed `7`.
--
-- GROUND TRUTH, HAND-DERIVED FROM THE DECLARATIONS, NOT CAPTURED: `core__foo` is
-- declared `: Int` and bound to `7` in lib/other.mdk; `import lib.other as O`
-- binds it as `O.core__foo`; so this prints `7` on run and on the built binary.
--
-- ⚠️ THE FIXTURE IS THE IDENTIFIER. `core__foo` is not decoration and must not be
-- "tidied" to a normal name -- rename it and this row still passes while testing
-- nothing. Same for its sibling fixture's `lib_plain__g`.
import lib.other as O

main = println O.core__foo
